A||N||11||fropuff||Why does the horn sound Japanese???||||10||
Z||000000||fropuff||10-28-2000||08:49 PM||||Hey, this has been bugging me ever since I got my GT back in April.  I am wondering why the horn on mine sounds like it came from a little Japanese car.  It might be the same on everyone else's, but why?  You come up with your engine screaming, your exhaust rumbling, and all it gives is, "beep, beep!"  I hate that!  I think I'm going to buy a replacement from JC Whitney; does anyone have any suggestions?  Thanks.||||reg||10
Z||000001||Philphine||10-28-2000||08:54 PM||||why is every thing metric? are the car companies in cahoots with sears to make you buy more tools even if you have an american car? ||||reg||1
Z||000002||fropuff||10-28-2000||08:57 PM||||That's true also.  I was taking the mirror out of my Cutlass today.  Pretty hard without taking the door panel out.  I just barely could fit my hand between the dew wipes.  I used a socket.  Took me at least an hour that it was metric!  Why doesn't one country or the other switch over so all of us can live in happiness?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>PS:  By the way, is my horn normal?  Does everyone else's sound the same?  Thanks.||||reg||1
